{"id": "EUVD-2026-26517", "enisaUuid": "2d659b29-3e08-3fce-a858-d32c807ecb91", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix OOB read in smb2_ioctl_query_info QUERY_INFO path\n\nsmb2_ioctl_query_info() has two response-copy branches: PASSTHRU_FSCTL\nand the default QUERY_INFO path.  The QUERY_INFO branch clamps\nqi.input_buffer_length to the server-reported OutputBufferLength and then\ncopies qi.input_buffer_length bytes from qi_rsp->Buffer to userspace, but\nit never verifies that the flexible-array payload actually fits within\nrsp_iov[1].iov_len.\n\nA malicious server can return OutputBufferLength larger than the actual\nQUERY_INFO response, causing copy_to_user() to walk past the response\nbuffer and expose adjacent kernel heap to userspace.\n\nGuard the QUERY_INFO copy with a bounds check on the actual Buffer\npayload.  Use struct_size(qi_rsp, Buffer, qi.input_buffer_length)\nrather than an open-coded addition so the guard cannot overflow on\n32-bit builds.", "datePublished": "2026-05-01T13:56:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:06:06", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e66bdc0704977ecee667a81d38255b579c2353d0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e203dbb5402897c43130fb171a2617008a91f45", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1dd757379997b71a328a4b591ffaf481acd0ead1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a34d456934fe42e4da5d2cc07787bf418bee99c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac2f14e4705d020f04e806efa0d49ab8dc2b145f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/078fae8f50adebb903ccf2252b44391324571e78", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/85fd46ee26a11841c670449508025965f61ce131", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a58c5af19ff0d6f44f6e9fe31e33a2c92223f77e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9grv-w29f-qpm9", "CVE-2026-31708"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2c9eab06-8f4c-37f2-8e20-f078f831c2c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3c8af232-7c36-389a-8350-93e6ae65aa51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.175"}, {"id": "4b371eea-af76-353b-a20a-785fd805c5e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5778c398713692a16150ae96e5c8270bab8399f <a58c5af19ff0d6f44f6e9fe31e33a2c92223f77e"}, {"id": "4bccdc58-09dc-3e2e-9074-7913cecc515c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5778c398713692a16150ae96e5c8270bab8399f <078fae8f50adebb903ccf2252b44391324571e78"}, {"id": "5f4aae9f-b53c-3ec5-bbc8-220d1417eeb2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5778c398713692a16150ae96e5c8270bab8399f <e66bdc0704977ecee667a81d38255b579c2353d0"}, {"id": "6aa23664-35d0-3911-a08e-9c869e5f25f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.2"}, {"id": "8b458167-6419-3e37-97cd-657045e279d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.84"}, {"id": "906892a8-d9d9-3955-80ec-2e6536e3c25b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "94889439-4b51-38ca-94b2-13d0184bbef4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.1"}, {"id": "984aaa46-ec76-3b53-9a19-b9f9d98c6556", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.25"}, {"id": "9bcc2972-daff-3d63-9054-9872b686305a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.136"}, {"id": "a88ff2e1-ed27-3a7b-b226-252e8a9218b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.259"}, {"id": "b85ae55f-48ca-3f6d-bee7-3695ea1b2f60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5778